<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-HENNESSY GOLD CUP RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-HENNESSY GOLD CUP RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the grade one Hennessy</p>
<p>Gold Cup steeplechase run over three miles (4.8 kms) at</p>
<p>Leoparstown on Sunday.</p>
<p> 1. Danoli	  6-1 (ridden by Tommy Treacy)</p>
<p> 2. Jodami	  5-1 (Norman Williamson)</p>
<p>3. Imperial Call Evens favourite (Conor O'Dwyer)</p>
<p>Eight ran.</p>
<p>Distances: One and a half lengths, 20 lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Dan O'Neill and  trained by Tom Foley in</p>
<p>County Carlow, Ireland.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 59,000 Irish pounds ($92,510)</p>
